# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your real key:   cp .env.example .env
#
# NOTE: .env is a convenience record for you — Claude Code does not read it.
# The ${SPOONACULAR_API_KEY} in .mcp.json expands from the environment Claude
# Code was launched in, so the key has to reach it one of two ways:
#
#   A) Set it in your shell before launching:
#        $env:SPOONACULAR_API_KEY = "..."                      # this session
#        [Environment]::SetEnvironmentVariable(                # persistent
#          "SPOONACULAR_API_KEY", "...", "User")
#
#   B) Put it in .claude/settings.local.json, which is also gitignored:
#        { "env": { "SPOONACULAR_API_KEY": "..." } }
#
# .env and .env.* are gitignored; .env.example is the deliberate exception.
# Never commit a real key.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Spoonacular Food API — recipe search + nutrition.
# Used by: recipe-researcher, nutrition-checker  (mcp__spoonacular__*)
#
# Where to get a key:
#   1. Register an account from https://spoonacular.com/food-api
#   2. Once logged in, the key is on the API console's Profile tab:
#      https://spoonacular.com/food-api/console#Profile
#
# Free plan: 50 POINTS per day, then calls stop until it resets. Points are not
# requests — the API meters per endpoint. A recipe search costs 1 point plus
# 0.01 per recipe returned (plus 0.025 per recipe when nutrition is included);
# a recipe lookup costs about 1 point. Because recipe-researcher deliberately
# over-supplies candidates 2-3x, one week-sized /plan-meals run lands roughly
# in the 15-25 point range — so budget about two full runs per day.
SPOONACULAR_API_KEY=your_spoonacular_api_key_here
